  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#33581\", \"PowerToys#42868\", \"PowerToys#28596\"], \"answer\": \"This request has been filed several times before. Two of the tickets (#33581 and #42868) were closed as duplicates of the main tracking issue #21313, 'A utility that disables the keyboard, mouse and touchscreen momentarily while physically cleaning the devices', so add your thumbs-up there rather than opening a new ticket. The tickets also record that the PowerToys team said in earlier discussions (#28596, #18066) that they had no plans to build a keyboard-lock utility and suggested simply locking the PC (Win+L) or turning it off. Another workaround from #44783 for a laptop's built-in keyboard is to disable it in Device Manager (Win+X > Device Manager > Keyboards > select the keyboard > Disable). Third-party tools such as KeyFreeze or Keyboard Clean Tool, which are mentioned in the tickets, can also lock input temporarily.\"}",
